{color:#bf2600}Contacting Driver Bs directly—such as to notify them of incorrect or expired documents—does carry some reclassification risk. That risk can be higher or lower depending on the nature and tone of the communication: If the contact is purely factual and clearly on behalf of Driver A, the risk is lower. If it  implies control, direction, or management by Bolt, the risk increases. {color}

