Hi [~accountid:712020:08485d64-da8c-4826-8ee4-512427d52ff5], just following up on this. Many thanks for flagging - I agree entirely that, although there is a legal basis, the form of the request is indeed problematic as it presumes a standard employment relationship, which is not the case for Bolt and its drivers. Bolt drivers are self-employed independent contractors using the platform. 

Therefore, we are not in a position to complete the “Employer Statement” portion of the EQ1 form. Doing so could imply an employment relationship where non exists. 

*Recommendation*

Subject to your thoughts, I recommend that we: 

* acknowledge the request and confirm that we are prepared to cooperate under the cited legal basis;
* clarify that Bolt does not maintain an employer-employee relationship with the individual in question, and that we cannot complete the form on that basis;
* offer to disclose the limited driver data we do hold in a format appropriate to our role as a platform provider, not as an employer (perhaps we can ask the DWP to offer alternatives);
* do not sign or complete the EQ1 form and instead attach an explanatory note and the relevant data as per the above points. 

Happy to discuss this further if helpful! Many thanks

