So I guess let’s consider them as a new supplier. 

Few further questions before legal review could be kicked off:

# *What are we buying?* The scope: “_Scale (Including API Plugin, Intent Data 25 Topics, Technographics Filter, Funding Filter, Job Change Filter & Job Change Alerts) with Unlimited Seats and 864,000 total Lusha One Credits for a fee of $43,200.00_”. One can make some assumptions based on this but it’s not entirely clear. From a quick look it’s also not defined in the Order Form, the [MSA|https://www.lusha.com/legal/master-subscription-agreement/], nor in the [Supplementary Terms|https://www.lusha.com/legal/fair-use-policy/]. *I assume we want the following, please correct me/ elaborate, and let me know what do you expect to be spelled out in the agreement documents explicitly to ensure we receive what is needed under the agreement,*

* access to the full breadth of Lusha’s database (contact, company, etc) for prospecting, lead enrichment and filtering; 
* all their (premium) features;
* API plugin to allow us to integrate Lusha's data services directly into our internal tools (just Salesforce?); 
* high(est) API usage limits;
* ability to track buyer intent across 25 predefined or custom categories, e.g. they should be able to indicate which companies are "in market" based on their content consumption (e.g., searching for “fleet management software”);
* whether and what other functionality (filters, alerts) we’d like to call out explicitly/ elaborate on in the agreement? 

# *What are the key risks you foresee under this agreement?*
# *Auto-renewal ok?*
# *Are we able to negotiate a long form agreement, i.e. agree and sign order form (and MSA and the supplementary terms as its annexes) subject to mutual amendments only (i.e. no unilateral amendments by Lusha to online terms in web w/o our approval).*

As a parallel track *privacy review* is needed. [~accountid:712020:b2a2738f-c1f1-447c-9b72-29851b5fed3e] please let me know if any amendments to the agreement are needed in relation to privacy matters. I assume per minimum we’d want Lusha to warrant that there is legal basis in place legitimizing planned data transfer and is liable for any misrepresentations on that front.

Cheers all,

A.

